-- title:
--   (4), p. 10 — Bayes rule: the ratio ∫h·P(Z|σ)d𝔾 / ∫P(Z|σ)d𝔾 is a version of E[h(Σ) | Z]
-- statement:
--   Let $(\Omega,\mathcal F,P)$ be a probability space carrying three mutually independent random variables: the truth $\theta\sim\mathcal N(\mu,s^2)$ with $s>0$, the accuracy $\Sigma\sim\mathbb G$, where $\mathbb G$ satisfies the standing assumption (a probability law with support in some $[\underline\sigma,\overline\sigma]$, $0<\underline\sigma$), and the noise $\epsilon\sim\mathcal N(0,1)$. Let $Z=\theta+\Sigma\epsilon$ be the post. Then for every bounded measurable $h:\mathbb R\to\mathbb R$,
--   $$\mathbb E\big[h(\Sigma)\,\big|\,Z\big]=\frac{\int h(\sigma)\,\psi\big((Z-\mu)^2,\sqrt{2(\sigma^2+s^2)}\big)\,d\mathbb G(\sigma)}{\int \psi\big((Z-\mu)^2,\sqrt{2(\sigma^2+s^2)}\big)\,d\mathbb G(\sigma)}\qquad P\text{-almost surely.}$$
--
--   This is the Bayes rule (4) of the paper, stated through posterior expectations: the posterior law of the accuracy given one post has density proportional to the likelihood (5) with respect to $\mathbb G$. It ties the ratio used in the definition of the screening scores to the probability model of the posts.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The conditional expectation is with respect to the σ-algebra generated by $Z$. The paper writes (4) as a posterior "density" $P(\Sigma=\sigma\mid Z)$; testing it against all bounded measurable $h$ is the measure-theoretic content of that identity.
-- source:
--   Allon, Drakopoulos & Manshadi, Information Inundation on Platforms and Implications, SSRN 3385627 (version of 2020-04-05), p. 10, proof of Proposition 1, eq. (4) (with eq. (1) and (5))

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_InfoInundation_Screening_Model
open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace InfoInundation.Screening

theorem eq_4 {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure P]
    (G : Measure ℝ) (hG : AccuracyLaw G) (μ s : ℝ) (hs : 0 < s) (θ Sig ε : Ω → ℝ)
    (hθ : Measurable θ) (hSig : Measurable Sig) (hε : Measurable ε)
    (hθlaw : P.map θ = gaussianReal μ (s ^ 2).toNNReal) (hSiglaw : P.map Sig = G)
    (hεlaw : P.map ε = gaussianReal 0 1) (hind : iIndepFun ![θ, Sig, ε] P)
    (h : ℝ → ℝ) (hh : Measurable h) (hhb : ∃ C : ℝ, ∀ x, |h x| ≤ C) :
    P[h ∘ Sig | MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => θ ω + Sig ω * ε ω) inferInstance]
      =ᵐ[P] fun ω => postExp G μ s (θ ω + Sig ω * ε ω) h := by sorry

end InfoInundation.Screening
